From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/a6xx: drop the boot bus vote once the GMU votes bandwidth

On GPUs whose GMU votes DDR bandwidth itself (a740 and later, info->bcms),
a6xx_gmu_resume() first sets the GPU OPP from the kernel through
a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw(), "a reasonable value for boot". The GMU starts at
the highest perf index, so on SM8550 that is the 680 MHz OPP's 16.5 GB/s.
a6xx_gmu_set_freq() then hands bandwidth to the GMU over HFI and skips
dev_pm_opp_set_opp() whenever bw_index is set, so nothing removes the
kernel's vote until the GMU is stopped. While the GPU stays powered, DDR
is held at its top frequency (4224 MHz), whatever the GPU's own load and
the GMU's vote: on the Odin 2 Portal idling in a launcher, DDR spent all
its time at 4224 MHz with the GPU at 220 MHz.

Remove the kernel's bus vote when the GMU takes it over, as
a6xx_gmu_stop() does ("Remove the bus vote"). The GPU OPP carries no
clock on GMU platforms, so a NULL OPP only drops the interconnect vote.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
index 276556267..61cb3b936 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_gmu.c
@@ -226,9 +226,12 @@ void a6xx_gmu_set_freq(struct msm_gpu *gpu, struct dev_pm_opp *opp,
 
 	if (!gmu->legacy) {
 		a6xx_hfi_set_freq(gmu, perf_index, bw_index);
-		/* With Bandwidth voting, we now vote for all resources, so skip OPP set */
-		if (!bw_index)
-			dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, opp);
+		/*
+		 * With Bandwidth voting the GMU votes for all resources: remove the bus
+		 * quota a6xx_gmu_set_initial_bw() set for boot, or it holds DDR at the
+		 * boot frequency's bandwidth for as long as the GPU stays powered
+		 */
+		dev_pm_opp_set_opp(&gpu->pdev->dev, bw_index ? NULL : opp);
 		return;
 	}
 
